<section class="ro-s ro-tm" id="timer"><div class="ro-w ro-tm-g"><div><p class="ro-ey">Tool one</p><h2 class="rv">Roast time calculator</h2><p class="ro-p">Choose the joint and its weight. We will give you an oven temperature, a cooking time, the internal temperature to aim for and how long to rest it.</p>
<label class="ro-lb" for="tm-m">What are you roasting?<select id="tm-m"><option value="ch">Whole chicken</option><option value="tu">Whole turkey</option><option value="br">Beef, rare</option><option value="bm" selected>Beef, medium</option><option value="bw">Beef, well done</option><option value="pk">Pork loin</option><option value="lb">Leg of lamb</option></select></label>
<label class="ro-lb" for="tm-w">Weight <output id="tm-wo">1.5 kg</output></label><input type="range" id="tm-w" min="0.5" max="8" step="0.1" value="1.5"><figure class="ro-tm-i rv rv-c"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1761315414257-e402bedaa43e?auto=format&fit=crop&w=640&h=340&q=75" alt="a roast joint with vegetables in a roasting tin" width="640" height="340" loading="lazy"></figure></div>
<div class="ro-tm-o"><svg class="ro-dial" viewBox="0 0 220 220" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="110" cy="110" r="100" class="dr"/><g id="tm-ticks"></g><g id="tm-kn"><circle cx="110" cy="110" r="64" class="dk"/><rect x="106" y="50" width="8" height="34" rx="4" class="dp"/></g><text x="110" y="118" id="tm-dt">180&deg;</text></svg>
<dl class="ro-read" aria-live="polite"><div><dt>Oven</dt><dd id="tm-o">180&deg;C</dd></div><div><dt>Roast for</dt><dd id="tm-t">1 h 0 min</dd></div><div><dt>Take it out at</dt><dd id="tm-i">60&deg;C</dd></div><div><dt>Rest for</dt><dd id="tm-r">20 min</dd></div></dl><p class="ro-note" id="tm-n"></p></div></div></section>

<section class="ro-s ro-pan" id="pan"><div class="ro-w"><div class="ro-pan-h"><p class="ro-ey">Tool two</p><h2 class="rv">Sheet pan planner</h2><p class="ro-p">Different vegetables need different times. Tick what you are roasting at 200&deg;C and we will tell you when each one goes onto the tray.</p></div>
<div class="ro-pan-g"><div class="ro-veg"><label><input type="checkbox" value="40" data-n="Potatoes" checked><span>Potatoes<em>40 min</em></span></label><label><input type="checkbox" value="45" data-n="Beetroot"><span>Beetroot<em>45 min</em></span></label><label><input type="checkbox" value="35" data-n="Carrots" checked><span>Carrots<em>35 min</em></span></label><label><input type="checkbox" value="35" data-n="Parsnips"><span>Parsnips<em>35 min</em></span></label><label><input type="checkbox" value="35" data-n="Squash"><span>Squash<em>35 min</em></span></label><label><input type="checkbox" value="30" data-n="Red onion" checked><span>Red onion<em>30 min</em></span></label><label><input type="checkbox" value="25" data-n="Cauliflower"><span>Cauliflower<em>25 min</em></span></label><label><input type="checkbox" value="25" data-n="Sprouts"><span>Sprouts<em>25 min</em></span></label><label><input type="checkbox" value="20" data-n="Peppers"><span>Peppers<em>20 min</em></span></label><label><input type="checkbox" value="18" data-n="Broccoli" checked><span>Broccoli<em>18 min</em></span></label><label><input type="checkbox" value="18" data-n="Courgette"><span>Courgette<em>18 min</em></span></label><label><input type="checkbox" value="12" data-n="Asparagus"><span>Asparagus<em>12 min</em></span></label><label><input type="checkbox" value="12" data-n="Cherry tomatoes"><span>Cherry tomatoes<em>12 min</em></span></label></div><div class="ro-pan-o"><div class="ro-tray" id="pn-t" aria-hidden="true"></div><ol class="ro-pl" id="pn-l" aria-live="polite"></ol></div></div></div></section>

<section class="ro-s ro-th"><div class="ro-w ro-th-g"><div class="ro-th-v"><div class="ro-therm" aria-hidden="true"><i id="th-f"></i><b id="th-v">40&deg;</b></div><figure class="ro-th-i rv rv-c"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1529692236671-f1f6cf9683ba?auto=format&fit=crop&w=560&h=380&q=75" alt="a roast steak being sliced to show a pink middle" width="560" height="380" loading="lazy"></figure></div><div><p class="ro-ey">Done is a number</p><h2 class="rv">Cook to temperature, not time</h2><p class="ro-p">A probe thermometer takes the guessing out of roasting. These are common target temperatures in the thickest part of the meat. The temperature keeps rising a few degrees while it rests.</p><ol class="ro-tls"><li class="ro-tl rv" data-t="52"><b>52&deg;C</b><span>Beef, rare</span><em>125&deg;F</em></li><li class="ro-tl rv" data-t="60"><b>60&deg;C</b><span>Lamb, medium</span><em>140&deg;F</em></li><li class="ro-tl rv" data-t="63"><b>63&deg;C</b><span>Pork</span><em>145&deg;F</em></li><li class="ro-tl rv" data-t="70"><b>70&deg;C</b><span>Beef, well done</span><em>158&deg;F</em></li><li class="ro-tl rv" data-t="74"><b>74&deg;C</b><span>Chicken &amp; turkey</span><em>165&deg;F</em></li><li class="ro-tl rv" data-t="93"><b>93&deg;C</b><span>Pulled pork</span><em>200&deg;F</em></li></ol><p class="ro-small">Guide figures only. Follow the food safety advice where you live.</p></div></div></section>

<section class="ro-s ro-fl"><div class="ro-w"><div class="ro-fl-h"><p class="ro-ey">Four small habits</p><h2 class="rv">Better roast vegetables</h2><p class="ro-p">Hover or tap a card to flip it.</p></div><div class="ro-fl-g"><div class="ro-fc rv" tabindex="0"><div class="ro-fc-in"><figure class="ro-fc-f"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1586195833898-170cabf110c5?auto=format&fit=crop&w=520&h=640&q=75" alt="roasted root vegetables on a tray" width="520" height="640" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Cut evenly</figcaption></figure><div class="ro-fc-b"><b>Cut evenly</b><p>Same-size pieces cook at the same speed. Aim for chunks about 3 cm across.</p></div></div></div><div class="ro-fc rv" tabindex="0"><div class="ro-fc-in"><figure class="ro-fc-f"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1636743716922-1884c23fb6f6?auto=format&fit=crop&w=520&h=640&q=75" alt="whole roasted carrots with herbs" width="520" height="640" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Give them space</figcaption></figure><div class="ro-fc-b"><b>Give them space</b><p>Crowded trays steam instead of roast. Use two trays rather than one full one.</p></div></div></div><div class="ro-fc rv" tabindex="0"><div class="ro-fc-in"><figure class="ro-fc-f"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1552845683-cfefc701e423?auto=format&fit=crop&w=520&h=640&q=75" alt="hasselback potatoes in a baking dish" width="520" height="640" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Hot fat first</figcaption></figure><div class="ro-fc-b"><b>Hot fat first</b><p>Heat the oil in the tin before the potatoes go in for crisp edges.</p></div></div></div><div class="ro-fc rv" tabindex="0"><div class="ro-fc-in"><figure class="ro-fc-f"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1606791510628-fc86850630bf?auto=format&fit=crop&w=520&h=640&q=75" alt="asparagus and lemon on a sheet pan" width="520" height="640" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Finish bright</figcaption></figure><div class="ro-fc-b"><b>Finish bright</b><p>Lemon, herbs or a little vinegar after roasting lift rich, caramelised flavours.</p></div></div></div></div></div></section>

